# search.zd — the one keyboard behaviour this language can implement.
#
# Everything the issue lists under "the parts that are genuinely hard" —
# focus trap, focus restore, roving tabindex, type-ahead — needs the
# program to move focus, and nothing can. What is left is the case where
# the focus is *already* where the keystroke has to be handled, and this is
# it: a reader typing in a filter box presses Escape and the box clears.
# The keystroke arrives at the field because the field is focused, the
# handler writes the field's own signal, and no focus moves. It is correct,
# it is complete, and it is the whole of the intersection.
#
# `field` is the `id`, and the caller supplies it rather than the widget
# inventing one. An id must be unique in a document and a component can be
# instantiated twice, so a widget that generated its own would produce two
# fields with one id and a `Label` pointing at whichever the browser found
# first. There is no way to make one that is unique per instance — the
# language has no identity for an instance — so the obligation is the
# caller's and it is in the signature where they will see it.
#
# `Label … controls is field` and not proximity. §16.3.6 requires
# `controls` for the reason `Image` requires `alt`: a `label` with no `for`
# names nothing and looks exactly like one that does.

component SearchField with query, label, field, class, inputClass
    Row class is class
        Label label, controls is field
        Input query, id is field, class is inputClass
            on keydown with press
                if press.key is "Escape"
                    set query to ""
        if query is not ""
            Button "Clear"
                on click
                    set query to ""
